<title>CHILE: Chile's Concha y Toro buys Argentine firm.</title>
<headline>Chile's Concha y Toro buys Argentine firm.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's largest winery Vina Concha y Toro SA said Friday it had acquired recently formed Argentine wine-maker Vina Patagonia, which has initial capital of $1.2 million.</p>
<p>The statement, which was filed with the Stocks and Values Superintendency, did not how much the Chilean winery would invest in the deal.</p>
<p>Vina Patagonia will produce and distribute wine in Argentina and abroad, Concha y Toro said.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago Newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
